# Keep LF everywhere, whatever core.autocrlf a Windows checkout uses. The
# web export's rules hash (tools/export_web.sh, game/net/net.gd) is a hash
# of the campaign/ and sim/ sources, so a CRLF checkout would export a build
# that refuses to join online campaigns made by an LF build; and the sh
# scripts break under Git Bash with CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.gd text eol=lf
*.gdshader text eol=lf
*.gdshaderinc text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.godot text eol=lf
*.import text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
